ou have  to take care of this thing over here  you're kind of a jerk  maybe you should fix this personality  trait that you've got going on over here  that's something that if we were  correctly aligned if we were thinking  straight we would recognize as a good  thing not as simply an attack on us so  Cicero begins talking about this in 24  and he says that varied and complex are  the experience as a friendship they  offer many causes for suspicion and  offense which is why sometimes to ignore  sometimes to make light up and sometimes  to endure but he says there's one cause  of offense in friendship which must be  encountered in order  that both the usefulness and loyalty of  friendship may be preserved for friends  frequently he doesn't just say every  once in a while  frequently must not only be advised and  the word here for advise Mon nd is also  warned the friends not to don't need to  have the positive things set out to them  how this is going to be a great thing  that you can plan to do they also need  some some warning but they also have to  be as he's saying rebuked or criticized  we have to say negative things to our  friends about their own actions choices  motivations character at some points and  this is going to be very important so he  says that both advice and rebuke you  have to be taken in in a certain way if  we don't do this we're actually letting  our friends down and that's that's not a  good thing so let's let's talk about  some of the things that he's saying here  Before we jump into the how to do it he  says that this preserves usefulness  utility toss and loyalty or fidelity  fides within the friendship so there  there's two different things going on  here  it is useful for us to hear criticism of  ourselves when that criticism is on  point because it allows us to avoid  screwing things up worse and it helps us  to perhaps either recognize that there's  a problem that needs to be attended to  or to have the resolve of finally  dealing with